  "kanji": "局",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 局\ntitle: bureau; office\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 7\nradical: 尸\nradicalNumber: 44\nonyomi: [キョク]\nkunyomi: [つぼね]\ndistractors: [同, 古, 写]\n---\n\n# 局 — bureau; office\n\n**Strokes:** 7 · **Key (radical):** 尸 (no. 44) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n局 appears in names of offices and service organizations. 郵便局 ゆうびんきょく is a post office;\n[薬局](../words/薬局.md) やっきょく is a pharmacy, not a generic office.\nThe first part of each word tells you what kind of organization or service is involved.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture a little 口-shaped service window tucked below the 尸 top and inside the turning outer line.\nThis uses the current shape for memory, not historical evidence.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キョク | on | [薬局](../words/薬局.md) やっきょく — pharmacy; 郵便局 ゆうびんきょく — post office |\n\nThe metadata also records つぼね; it is not the reading used in these service words.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [薬局](../words/薬局.md) やっきょく — pharmacy\n- 郵便局 ゆうびんきょく — post office\n- 放送局 ほうそうきょく — broadcasting station; broadcaster\n\n## Notes\n\n薬局 is やっきょく, with a small っ before きょ.\n[同](同.md) and [古](古.md) also contain a clear 口, but their upper and outer lines are different.\n[写](写.md) is a looser visual comparison: it has a covering top and folded lower strokes, not the enclosed 口 of 局.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project);\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1538200, 1542430, 1516760.\n",
